        "original_id": "9dacefa0-638e-5c00-9a1b-704db0890a3e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Cortinarius kioloensis\n- Places: Higgins Creek, Kioloa State Forest, Batemans Bay, southern New South Wales, New South Wales, Australia, Deua National Park, Moruya, Narooma\n- Topics: type specimen collection, town location, nearby coastal towns\n\nFacts:\n- On 22 June 1980, the type specimen of Cortinarius kioloensis was collected along Higgins Creek in Kioloa State Forest near Batemans Bay in southern New South Wales.\n- Batemans Bay is a town in the South Coast region of New South Wales, Australia.\n- Deua National Park has nearby coastal towns including Batemans Bay, Moruya, and Narooma.",
